    "slug": "minor-caged-boxes-and-forms",
    "title": "Boxes and Forms: Two Maps of the Same Dots",
    "summary": "CAGED and the numbered Boxes are two different tilings of the identical minor pentatonic dots, and exactly two of the five pairs happen to coincide because two of their anchor offsets agree.",
    "tags": ["caged", "minor"],
    "readingTimeMin": 5,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Five windows, joined up. Every overlap between neighbouring windows holds all five notes of the scale, and three of the four hold them one per string. "
        },
        {
          "text": "Chapter 2 proved this in chord tones",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "minor-caged-five-shapes-one-neck"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "; this is the same claim with the whole scale in it."
        }
      ]
    },
